  "term": "Northern blot",
  "definition": "Northern blot is a laboratory method used to detect specific RNA molecules in a sample. It works by separating extracted RNA on a gel, transferring it to a membrane, and using a complementary labeled DNA or RNA probe to show whether the target RNA is present.",
